  "description": "DAWBEK crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C72 H80 Er6 N8 O20 2+,2(Cl1 1-),C2 H6 O1,2(C1 H4 O1),0.5(H2 O1). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er1A (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er2A (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er3A (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er5 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er6 (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er4A (Er) has 7 O neighbors; Er5A (Er) has 6 O neighbors; Er6A (Er) has 6 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 18 pairs, 2 components; largest component is a network with cycles with approximately planar metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.512-3.972 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 92.34-113.41°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Er6(L2)4(OH)4(EtOH)2(H2O)2]·2Cl·2EtOH·MeOH·H2O (C76H96N8O24Cl2Er6). Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article formula), 4 OH (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)), 2 H2O (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
  "interpretation_limit": "Oxidation states, nuclearity, oxo/hydroxo bridging, core charge and ligand identities/counts require article/SI or manual verification; atom-site counts are asymmetric-unit counts, not molecular stoichiometry. Graph topology is limited to identity-symmetry bonds in the CIF table. Approximate shape is based only on bridge-unwrapped metal-site coordinates in the largest component; symmetry-related bonds or periodic structures require manual crystallographic review. Empirical formulas alone do not establish unique oxidation-state assignments or ligand connectivity; annotations above reproduce explicit structural notation only.",
